# Tawjeh Level 2 — Advanced .NET Backend

## Real-World Backend Project Roadmap

**Duration:** 3 Months
**Structure:** 6 Sprints × 2 Weeks
**Expected Commitment:** ~15 Hours/Week
**Total:** ~180 Hours
**Project Type:** Production-Style Modular Monolith REST API
**Primary Focus:** Advanced .NET Backend Engineering, Architecture, Business Logic, Data Access, Security, Performance, Production Practices

---

# 🎯 Level Goal

The goal of Level 2 is to move the learner beyond building CRUD APIs and introduce the mindset required to build a **real-world backend system**.

By the end of the level, the learner should be able to:

* Design a maintainable backend architecture.
* Model a non-trivial business domain.
* Build APIs around real use cases rather than database tables.
* Apply Clean Architecture appropriately.
* Use CQRS and MediatR where they provide value.
* Implement authentication and authorization.
* Build meaningful business rules and domain behavior.
* Design efficient EF Core queries.
* Handle pagination, filtering, searching, sorting, and concurrency.
* Understand and improve backend performance.
* Implement caching when appropriate.
* Build background processing and scheduled operations.
* Integrate external services.
* Implement structured logging and production-oriented error handling.
* Integrate an external AI service into a backend system.
* Write meaningful Unit Tests.
* Containerize the application with Docker.
* Deploy the backend.
* Explain the architectural and engineering decisions made throughout the project.

The learner is not expected to memorize technologies.

The objective is to understand **why a particular solution is needed, how it works, and when it should or should not be used.**

