# 🧩 Core Domain

## Organization

An organization contains multiple teams and projects.

## Team

A team belongs to an organization and contains users with different responsibilities.

## Project

A project belongs to an organization and contains members, tasks, sprints, and activity.

## Project Member

A user can participate in a project with a specific role.

## Task

A task belongs to a project and can contain:

* Title
* Description
* Status
* Priority
* Creator
* Assignee
* Due Date
* Labels
* Comments
* Dependencies
* Time Entries

## Task Status

Example:

```text
Todo
InProgress
Blocked
Completed
Cancelled
```

## Sprint

A project can contain multiple sprints.

Each sprint has:

* Name
* Start Date
* End Date
* Tasks

## Task Dependency

A task may depend on another task.

Example:

```text
Implement Authentication
        ↓
Implement Authorization
        ↓
Implement Project Permissions
```

## Comment

Users can comment on tasks.

## Time Entry

Users can record the amount of time spent working on tasks.

## Notification

The system can notify users about important events.

Examples:

* Task assigned
* Task completed
* Comment added
* Deadline approaching

## Activity

The system records important project actions.

Examples:

```text
User assigned Task #15 to Ahmed
User changed Task #15 status to Completed
User added Mohamed to Project X
```

